(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #90 — the window. The store-back has to happen at the
 reallocation and not when the call returns: between the two, the callee can
 call another function that reaches the same buffer through its global
 mirror, and that read must not land in the block that was just freed.
 Before the fix each watch segfaulted INSIDE the call, after the literal
 part of its own line had already been printed.

 The second half is the same window one frame deeper: the buffer is grown
 through a parameter that is itself a parameter, so the new pointer has to
 reach the buffer's OWNER at the reallocation rather than one return at a
 time. A watcher called from down there sees it, or it sees freed memory.)

a buffer called transcript is "start".
a buffer called ledger is "start".

To 'watch the transcript'.
    Print "the watcher reads: {transcript's size}".

To 'watch the ledger'.
    Print "the watcher reads: {ledger's size}".

To 'pad out then look' with a buffer called sink.
    'watch the transcript'.
    a number called appended is 0.
    While appended is less than 600,
        append "0123456789" to sink,
        Set appended to appended add 1.
    'watch the transcript'.

To 'pad out deeper then look' with a buffer called sink.
    a number called appended is 0.
    While appended is less than 600,
        append "0123456789" to sink,
        Set appended to appended add 1.
    'watch the ledger'.

To 'hand it on' with a buffer called sink.
    'pad out deeper then look' of sink.

'pad out then look' of transcript.
Print "the caller reads: {transcript's size}".

'hand it on' of ledger.
Print "the ledger's owner reads: {ledger's size}".
